/* ---------- toast (theme + tray toggles now live in the nav) ---------- */
.hint{position:fixed;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);bottom:16px;background:var(--fg);color:var(--bg);padding:10px 16px;border-radius:var(--r);font:var(--f1) var(--mono);opacity:0;transition:.2s;pointer-events:none;z-index:70;max-width:92vw;word-break:break-all}
.hint.show{opacity:.96}
/* the stale-build offer — pinned under the top edge, never over the tab he is
   reading, and it wraps rather than pushing anything off a phone screen. */
#stalebuild{position:fixed;top:0;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);z-index:69;display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;background:#c9772e;color:#fff;padding:7px 12px;border-radius:0 0 var(--r) var(--r);font-size:var(--f1);box-shadow:0 2px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.25);max-width:94vw;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center}
#stalebuild .chip{background:rgba(255,255,255,.18);border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.45);color:#fff}
#stalebuild .chip:hover{background:rgba(255,255,255,.32)}
</style>

<nav id="nav">
  <span class="brand"><span class="mark">⎈</span>helm</span>
  <!-- FOUR PAGES, the owner's words: "are board and work and the 'work
       landing' section at the top of history (which is really the kanban
       board) really all separate things? what if it was just work and
       history and history focuses on signing stuff", and "since chat already
       needs no sub menu, maybe board needs no submenu either and history just
       moves to the 4th item in the top level menu?". So WORK is one page (the
       board, the work tab, the scheduler and the land pipeline), CHAT is
       unchanged, FLEET keeps its sections, and HISTORY is the signing ledger.
       Only Fleet has a section row. Every retired hash (#board, #helm,
       #scheduler, #ledger) still lands on the page that took it over, through
       canonView; AREA_OF in the nav script is the one map. -->
  <div class="navareas">
    <button class="navarea on" data-a="work">Work</button>
    <button class="navarea" data-a="chat">Chat</button>
    <button class="navarea" data-a="fleet">Fleet</button>
    <button class="navarea" data-a="history">History</button>
  </div>
  <span class="spacer"></span>
  <div class="stats" id="navstats"></div>
  <button class="icon" id="themetog" title="toggle light / dark">◐</button>
  <button class="icon" id="trayBtn" title="team tray — collect seats">⊞</button>
  <!-- the section row of the OPEN area. Only Fleet has one; the row is hidden
       (.solo) while a single-page area is open. The Fleet group stays in the
       document while closed, so its badges keep rendering and every data-v
       stays queryable. -->
  <div class="navtabs solo">
    <div class="navsec" data-a="fleet">
      <button class="navtab" data-v="quota">credit</button>
      <button class="navtab" data-v="roster">seats</button>
      <button class="navtab" data-v="sessions">sessions</button>
      <button class="navtab" data-v="configs">configs</button>
      <button class="navtab" data-v="boxes">boxes</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</nav>
<!-- THE STALE-PAGE TELL. This tab is long-lived and the server is assembled
     fresh per request, so the page he is reading can be hours older than the
     one helm would serve — he read a card for hours that a newer build had
     already moved, and reported what the old page showed. Nothing on the
     console could tell him, because nothing on the console knew. It is an
     OFFER and never an act: a console that reloaded itself would throw away
     whatever he was in the middle of typing. -->
<div id="stalebuild" hidden>
  <span>helm has changed since you opened this page</span>
  <button class="chip" id="stalereload">reload it</button>
  <button class="chip" id="stalehide" title="keep reading this version">not now</button>
</div>

<div class="wrap">

